The focused suite now compiles and 38/39 tests pass. The remaining failure is useful: teardown was spending the entire 10-second transport-close budget trying to drain an intentionally non-cooperative upload source. I’m changing owned-operation reconciliation to a short grace capped by the transport deadline; cooperative children still retire before snapshot, while genuinely non-cooperative work remains explicitly counted and close stays prompt.
